INTERESTING! This is a Deno quirk - in Deno, even reassigning a const variable throws "Assignment to constant variable"! This is different from standard V8/Node behavior!

The issue is that `H_rad = normalizeAngle(H_rad);` is trying to reassign a `const` variable, which Deno doesn't allow mid-module, even though it's just one second after the original assignment.

The fix is to use a different variable name:
[0m$ [0mcd work/weak/opencode/rally-3d-sun-0 && deno run testVar.js
error: Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.
  x = x + 1;
    ^
    at test1 (file://work/weak/opencode/rally-3d-sun-0/testVar.js:6:5)
    at file://work/weak/opencode/rally-3d-sun-0/testVar.js:10:24
> build · bench-model
Hmm, it seems I can't reassign in Deno at all. Let me use let instead of const for D5119 optimization:
