At Seattle's latitude (47.6°N) on June 21 (declination = +23.4°), at local noon:
altitude = 90 - latitude + declination = 90 - 47.6 + 23.4 = 65.8°

But I'm getting negative values! The hour angle calculation must be wrong - specifically, I think the result is giving me the wrong local time offset.

